%description:

Tcp.delayedAckTimeout:value -- the delayed ACK of a lone segment comes after the timeout.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with delayedAcksEnabled, the longest delay of an ACK (RFC 9293 MUST-40:
less than 0.5 s)".

The classes: value (a time above 0; 100ms here, the default is 200ms), zero (0s). The code
schedules the delayed ACK timer with this time (TcpAlgorithmBase::receiveSeqChanged()); a
negative time has no check (a finding of the catalog). This test separates "value" from
"zero": with 0s, the ACK goes in the same instant.

Host under test: host2, the receiver, with the delayed ACK. Peer: host1 sends one segment of
100 bytes. Observation: level 1, the ACK of host2: none in the first 99 ms after the arrival,
one in the next 2 ms.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# class: value
%# value: 100ms
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDelayedAckTimeoutValue")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the segment of 100 bytes at host2")
                  .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                   .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                   .describe("an ACK of host2 before the timeout")
                   .within(0.099))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .describe("the delayed ACK of host2, at the timeout")
                  .within(0.002));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAckTimeoutValue compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout = 100ms    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDelayedAckTimeoutValue: PASS
